{
  "manufacturer": "Marley Engineered Products",
  "manufacturer_slug": "marley-engineered-products",
  "model": "Smart Series Plus digital heater controller (BACnet MS/TP)",
  "model_slug": "smart-series-plus",
  "aliases": [
    "Smart Series Plus",
    "Smart-Series Plus",
    "5200-11256-004",
    "Marley unit heater BACnet controller"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Thermostat / controller for cabinet unit heaters",
  "applies_to": "Marley Engineered Products Smart Series Plus digital controls for cabinet and unit heaters, on BACnet MS/TP.",
  "summary": "The Smart Series Plus is a wall-mount digital controller for Marley Engineered Products heaters, built on Honeywell's BACnet FF (TB3026B) platform with application 5 loaded. It joins BACnet MS/TP and exposes the platform's setpoint, display, occupancy and schedule objects plus the heater application's settings: output enable, fan mode, standby, heating loop gains, fan start/stop and BMS scheduling options.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 9999,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "The appendix gives each object a label in an 'Object Name' column, but its property tables say the Object_Name property reads 'AV-nnn' / 'BV-nnn' / 'MV-nnn' for most objects. The labels are used as names here; a scan may show the AV-nnn form.",
    "Physical I/O objects (AI 0-2, AO 0-7, BI 0-2, BO 0-5) and the general-use AV 0-89 / BV 0-63 depend on the loaded application (DDC file); they are not listed here except where the guide names them.",
    "BV 40 (general-use range) is the occupancy command and supports a priority array.",
    "Access comes from the appendix where it has an access column; otherwise it is inferred (displayed/sensed/current/status points and multistates read-only, others writable).",
    "The ordered list in this guide marks the humidity, UV-lamp and several display objects RESERVED; they are left out. Application points (AV 17-79, BV 2-56) come from the guide's setup tables (Tables 21, 23 and 24), with defaults in the descriptions.",
    "Output Enable (BV 2) must be set ON at start-up or the relays stay off.",
    "The object set is the Honeywell BACnet FF platform; see the Honeywell TB3026B list for the full platform including humidity objects."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Smart Series Plus Installation and Operations Guide (English section, Appendix A and B)",
    "doc_number": "5200-11256-004",
    "revision_date": "10/23",
    "url": "https://www.marleymep.com/wp-content/uploads/5200-11256-004.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set Output Enable (BV 2) ON, the MS/TP MAC and device instance (ISU 800-804), and decide between the internal schedule and BMS scheduling (BV 56). Then write occupancy (BV 40) and the occupied setpoint AV 90, and read the room temperature, active heating setpoint and occupied status.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 2",
        "name": "Output Enable",
        "why": "Output enable; must be ON for the heater to run"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 56",
        "name": "Enable BMS Scheduling",
        "why": "Enable BMS scheduling (overrides internal schedule)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 90",
        "name": "Setpoint (SP)",
        "why": "Occupied space setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 96",
        "name": "Unoccupied Heating SP",
        "why": "Unoccupied heating setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 9",
        "name": "Enable Communication Failure",
        "why": "Go occupied on MS/TP comm failure"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 104",
        "name": "Sensed Room Temperature",
        "why": "Room temperature (built-in sensor)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 100",
        "name": "Current Heating SP",
        "why": "Active heating setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 67",
        "name": "Occupied/Unoccupied Status",
        "why": "Occupied / unoccupied status"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "BV 2 Output Enable must be ON. With BV 56 active the BMS schedules occupancy (BV 40, priority array) instead of the internal schedule.",
    "heartbeat": "BV 9 Enable Communication Failure: when active the controller falls back to occupied if MS/TP communication fails.",
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Factory defaults: MS/TP MAC 0 (valid 0-127), device instance 0009999 (valid 0-4194302).",
      "MS/TP MAC is ISU 800 (0-127); device instance is entered in parts through ISU 801-804.",
      "Application selection AV 49 must stay at 5 for Marley heaters."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Table 24 marks several display objects 'Do Not Change'; leave them at their defaults.",
      "SYSTEM block OFF (BV 102 visible) overrides scheduled occupied to unoccupied."
    ]
  },
